<!--
  rev_applicanttype - PLACEHOLDER VALUES, TO CONFIRM.

  The raw export (col 35, "Are you") proves the live form asks the applicant to classify
  themselves, but the header carries no option list and the data row is empty, so the real
  values are NOT known. docs/Import/grant-application-data-model-v0.2.md records the same gap:
  "Applicant type | Choice | Values behind 'Are you...' to confirm."

  The four options below are inferred from the charity's own description of who it serves
  (SDD section 1: unpaid carers and the disabled people they care for) and from the structure of
  the form itself, which branches into an applicant condition block (cols 53-67) and a
  support-recipient condition block (cols 68-94). They are a placeholder, not a decision.

  CONFIRM WITH EMILY BEFORE PRD. This column is a reporting dimension, so a wrong option list
  produces wrong figures rather than a visible failure.
-->
<optionset Name="rev_applicanttype" localizedName="Applicant Type">
  <OptionSetType>picklist</OptionSetType>
  <IsGlobal>1</IsGlobal>
  <IntroducedVersion>1.0.0.0</IntroducedVersion>
  <IsCustomizable>1</IsCustomizable>
  <options>
    <option value="1">
      <labels>
        <label description="A disabled person applying for myself" languagecode="1033" />
